{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having trouble keeping food down and have some pain. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. For the past two days, I’ve had this constant burning pain in my upper belly that goes up into my chest. It feels like when I had an ulcer before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Is it worse after eating? And have you been able to keep anything down?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can only drink water and protein shakes. Solids make me nauseous. I did vomit once when I got to the ER—dark brown, not bright red, but scary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be old blood. We’ll check things carefully. You mentioned this feels like your past ulcer—have you had gastrojejunal ulcers before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, after my gastric bypass. And I still have the G-tube for feeds because of low blood sugar issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. Given your history, we’re going to keep you NPO for now—nothing by mouth except sips of water. We’ll start IV fluids and run some tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But I’m worried about my blood sugars—they’ve been low at night. That’s why I restarted tube feeds yesterday, but it didn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor your glucose closely. For now, we’ll give you dextrose in your IV to keep your sugars stable. We’ll also check your cortisol since you have a history of adrenal issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-07-19 19:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-07-20 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs came back mostly normal—no signs of infection or pancreatitis. Your hemoglobin is a bit low, but stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-07-20 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Any idea what’s causing the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-07-20 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not sure yet. You’re scheduled for an upper GI study today with contrast to check for any blockages, leaks, or ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-07-20 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt? I’m a little anxious about it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-07-20 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not painful. You’ll drink a liquid that shows up on X-ray, and we’ll watch how it moves. It helps us see what’s going on inside."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-07-20 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-07-20 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The upper GI is back—good news. No leaks, no blockages, and no strictures. Your anatomy looks intact."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-07-20 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why am I still in pain and nauseous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-07-20 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could still be related to your past ulcers or delayed gastric emptying. We’re going to restart your tube feeds slowly and try a different formula."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-07-20 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on Vivonex before. Can we try that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-07-20 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with Vivonex at a low rate, but if nausea continues, we may switch to something more concentrated like Jevity 1.5."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-07-20 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my nausea meds—can we adjust them? Zofran isn’t helping as much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-07-20 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can switch to prochlorperazine, which sometimes works better for people with your history. We’ll give it as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-07-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. We started the tube feeds yesterday at 30 mL/hr, but you had nausea above that rate. Today, we’re going to try Jevity 1.5 at a slower rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-07-21 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that the thicker one? I’ve used it before at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-07-21 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, more calories per mL. We’ll go slow and increase only if you tolerate it. We also added erythromycin—it helps with stomach motility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-07-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Erythromycin? Isn’t that an antibiotic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-07-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is, but at low doses, it acts like a stomach stimulant. Helps move things along, which might reduce nausea and fullness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-07-21 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, okay. That sounds helpful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-07-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. You’ve been on Jevity 1.5 at 45 mL/hr for the past 12 hours with minimal nausea. That’s your goal rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-07-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I didn’t even notice. I feel less bloated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-07-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your blood sugars are stable too, so we’re weaning off the dextrose IV. You’ll stay on the tube feeds at home at this rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-07-22 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I ever eat by mouth again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-07-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but slowly. Right now, your stomach isn’t emptying well. We’ll focus on nutrition through the tube and reassess later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-07-23 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two full days on goal feeds with no nausea or pain. We’re calling this a success."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-07-23 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s such a relief. Can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-07-23 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge in a day or two. We need to make sure you can manage the feeds at home and have your prescriptions ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-07-23 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need the new meds—prochlorperazine and erythromycin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-07-23 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Erythromycin for a few weeks to help with motility, and prochlorperazine as needed for nausea. Keep taking your pantoprazole and sucralfate for ulcer prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-07-24 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge team confirmed your home nursing support. They’ll help you set up the feeding pump."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-07-24 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was nervous about doing it alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-07-24 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’ll train you and your caregiver. You’ll also follow up with your surgeon and primary team soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-07-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. Your labs are stable, you’re walking well, and you’ve had no symptoms. We’re clearing you for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-07-25 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was really worried this was something serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-07-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s related to delayed gastric emptying and your history of ulcers. The new formula and motility agent seem to have helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-07-26 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check-in. Any nausea or pain last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-07-26 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "None. Slept well, feeds ran smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-07-26 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll write your discharge orders this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we’re finalizing your discharge. You’ll go home on Jevity 1.5 at 45 mL/hr continuously, plus bolus 200 mL every six hours if you want."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take erythromycin four times a day for now, prochlorperazine as needed for nausea, and continue your regular meds like pantoprazole and sucralfate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if I start feeling pain again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor. If it’s severe, or if you vomit blood or have black stools, go to the ER. Also watch for fever or dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And no driving with the pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Only take pain meds if needed, and don’t drive while on them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll have my sister help at first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-07-27 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good plan. You’re alert, walking independently, and medically stable—ready for home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-07-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge paperwork is ready. You’ll leave in an hour or so once the pharmacy sends your prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-07-28 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-07-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep up with your follow-up appointments, take your meds, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2174-07-28 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2174-07-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-07-19 19:22:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-07-28 11:08:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with a two-day history of epigastric and mid-abdominal pain, nausea, and intolerance to oral intake, with symptoms reminiscent of a prior gastrojejunal ulcer. She was kept NPO initially, started on IV dextrose for glucose stability, and underwent an upper GI series that showed no leak, stricture, or obstruction. Tube feeds were restarted with Vivonex but poorly tolerated; she transitioned successfully to Jevity 1.5 at 45 mL/hr with improved tolerance. Erythromycin was added to enhance gastric motility, and her antiemetic was changed from ondansetron to prochlorperazine with good effect. She remained hemodynamically stable, achieved goal enteral nutrition, and was discharged home on a regimen of continuous and bolus tube feeding, erythromycin, and PRN prochlorperazine, with follow-up planned.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastrojejunal ulcer, unspecified as acute or chronic, without hemorrhage or perforation",
      "Other adrenocortical insufficiency",
      "Postgastric surgery syndromes",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 34.0-34.9, adult",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Polycystic ovarian syndrome",
      "Gastrostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
